<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher icon.

  All three layers come from the supplied artwork:
    background  - a flat colour lifting the dark navy out of the source PNG
    foreground  - the neon artwork, shipped as ic_launcher_foreground.png in
                  every density rather than as a vector
    monochrome   - the same foreground, used by Android 13+ themed icons

  The foreground is the source PNG at full bleed, 108dp. That is deliberate and
  it is what makes the icon look the same on every launcher instead of being
  cropped differently by each mask: the design runs to the edge of the canvas,
  so there is no artwork sitting outside the 18dp that a circular or squircle
  mask discards. Anything inset here would show up as a gap on some launchers
  and not on others, which is the problem this icon was meant to fix.

  Monochrome points at the colour foreground. Android 13 tints it by alpha, and
  the neon art is drawn light on the dark navy field, so the alpha channel
  carries the shape on its own. The themed icon is therefore the same Delta
  mark rather than a filled square.

  The background colour is the exact navy sampled from the PNG (RGB 5,9,26).
  It has to be exact: the foreground is that same artwork at full bleed, so any
  mismatch shows as a seam around the edge on every launcher that draws the
  background layer at all.
-->
<adaptive-icon xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <background android:drawable="@color/ic_launcher_background" />
    <foreground android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
    <monochrome android:drawable="@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground" />
</adaptive-icon>